      "phase": 11,
      "change": "canonical_config.policy gained mlp_obs_feat_dim=256, restoring the MLP arm's observation MLP from VariDP (docs/final-plan.md §6 B2); no scientific hyperparameter changed"
    },
    {
      "phase": 17,
      "change": "canonical_config.train gained betas=[0.95,0.999], which was hardcoded in the trainer; the value is unchanged and now resolves through baseline.toml"
    },
    {
      "phase": 17,
      "change": "canonical_config.train.num_workers 8 -> 4 to fit the 4 CPUs per GPU job on the HKU cluster; batches are drawn from (seed, step), so training is unchanged"
    },
    {
      "phase": 18,
      "change": "canonical_config.train.num_workers 4 -> 3 because one dual-GPU Slurm job runs two trainers on 8 CPUs; batches are drawn from (seed, step), so training is unchanged"
    },
    {
      "phase": 19,
      "change": "canonical_config.data gained the runtime switch preload=false (lazy HDF5 reads, as before); preloading only changes where the same bytes are read from, so training is unchanged"
    },
    {
      "phase": 20,
      "change": "canonical_config.vision gained pool=avg (the global average pooling the encoder always used) and num_keypoints=32 (read only by the optional spatial_softmax head); no scientific hyperparameter changed"
    },
    {
      "phase": 21,
      "change": "canonical_config.data.preload false -> true: RGB is decoded into RAM once instead of re-inflating gzip chunks per window (2.34x steps/s, job 135722); windows are bit-identical, and completion and resume ignore data.preload, so recorded lazy runs stay completed and resumable"
    }
